  37:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** *
  38:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** * @section DESCRIPTION
  39:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** *
  40:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** * Generic ring buffer library for deeply embedded system.
  41:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** * It uses a data store whose size is a power of 2 (8, 16, 32, 64, ...)
  42:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** * and doesn't waste any data bytes.  It has very low overhead, and
  43:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** * utilizes modulo for indexing the data in the data store.
  44:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** * It uses separate variables for consumer and producer so it can
  45:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** * be used in multithreaded environment.
  46:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** *
  47:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** * See the unit tests for usage examples.
  48:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** *
  49:../src/middleware/bacnet/src/ringbuf.c **** */
